  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The numbers \\(x,\\) \\(y,\\) \\(z\\) are proportional to \\(2,\\) \\(3,\\) \\(5.\\) The sum of \\(x,\\) \\(y,\\) and \\(z\\) is \\(100.\\) The number \\(y\\) is given by the equation \\(y=ax-10.\\) Then \\(a\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac23\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac52\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(4\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "2"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1957-p8.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(x=2t,\\) \\(y=3t,\\) and \\(z=5t.\\) Since \\(10t=100,\\) we get \\(t=10,\\) so \\(x=20\\) and \\(y=30.\\) Thus \\[ 30=20a-10, \\] and \\(a=2.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Write \\(x,y,z\\) as \\(2t,3t,5t\\)",
        "Their sum determines \\(t\\), after which substitute \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) into the given equation"
      ],
